patch=1,EE,00166A58,word,087F0E30   // traffic update, once per frame: keep the lap message registered (was b 0x00166A80)
// ===== Traffic Attack traffic spread, density and direction (from bebf8793_traffic_spread.pnach) =====
// Seed: CB3TrafficSystem::ResetMemberVariables (0x001632C0) mixes the fixed seed with COP0 Count; the replay
// (stage state 0xC, after logic->StartReplay) reuses the seed of the race instead of drawing a new one.
// Spread: FillLaneSection placed car i at i*spacing*rand; now (i+rand)*spacing. Sections with rate > 0 but
// < 0.5 expected cars got none; now at least K_MIN.
// Zero-rate lanes (16% of the valve lanes on the track checked): FillLaneSection, Valve::Update and
// PrepareGenerationTimes run with the rates of another lane of the same valve (or DEFRATES); the pointers
// are restored right after each call, so nothing is written to the track data.
// v5: lane stretches no sector lists are filled when 150-600 m ahead (map built once per race).
// v4: prefill - while the game has no pending section, the fill sections of the NEXT sector are filled one per
// frame; when the player enters it, the game skips the sections already filled (hooks 0x001646A8/0x00164748/0x00164A14).
// v3: lanes below K_FLOOR cars/min (sum of categories) run with a scaled copy of their rates (floor, not a
// multiplier: lanes at or above the floor are untouched). Same swap-and-restore as the zero-rate lanes.
// v2 fix: the MIN cave no longer touches t0 (FillLaneSection argument still live there).
// Caves 01FCA000-01FCA67F (free part of the Traffic Attack arena). Generated by mk_spread5.py.
